rds (A, Red Joker). Breaking this straight would result in a disjointed hand with many weak singles. Therefore, playing the straight is the best opening move to maximize card efficiency and clear the hand quickly.\n\nReason: This move utilizes the isolated low cards (3, 5, 7, 9) in a 7-card straight, leaving a well-structured hand with pairs, a pair sequence, and high cards. It is the most efficient way to reduce the card count and maintain control.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦3", "♥4", "♣5", "♠6", "♦7", "♠8", "♠9"]}'}
