nitiative.\n\n**The Strategic Choice**\n\nI need to protect my hand. My hand structure depends on me getting the lead, so I must play the Red Joker to take control. This move is necessary to unlock my best hand potential. Despite the high price of the joker, it is my only option to stay competitive in this game.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: My hand is structured around a strong sequence of pairs (10-10, J-J, Q-Q) and several isolated pairs (4-4, 8-8). I lack any Kings, Aces, or 2s to bridge the gap between the played Queen and my Red Joker. The Next Player (Right) has only 7 cards left and is a major threat. If I pass, the Previous Player (Left, Right\'s partner) will likely pass to let Right retain the lead, potentially allowing Right to play a combination I cannot defend against (like a straight or triplet). To win, I must seize the initiative to play my sequence of pairs, which clears half my hand at once.\n\nReason: The Red Joker is the only card I have that can beat the Queen. Taking the lead is crucial to play the 1010-JJ-QQ sequence of pairs, which is my primary win condition. Allowing the opponent with 7 cards to continue unchallenged is too dangerous, and I cannot rely on the other opponent to interfere.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["RedJoker"]}'}
